1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,000
If you shop for clothes in Seoul and skip one simple step,

2
00:00:04,000 --> 00:00:08,000
you're literally leaving money on the table.

3
00:00:08,000 --> 00:00:15,000
By the end, you'll know how to get it back — and how much you'll actually save.

4
00:00:15,000 --> 00:00:22,000
In Korea, almost everything you buy includes a ten percent VAT.

5
00:00:22,000 --> 00:00:30,000
But as a foreign tourist, you're allowed to get most of that back.

6
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:38,000
It's the tourist tax refund — and it works on fashion, shoes, bags, and skincare.

7
00:00:38,000 --> 00:00:50,000
To qualify: a foreign visitor, staying under six months, not working in Korea.

8
00:00:50,000 --> 00:01:00,000
Most travelers forget it. Don't be one of them.

9
00:01:00,000 --> 00:01:10,000
There are two ways. The easiest is instant refund.

10
00:01:10,000 --> 00:01:22,000
If a single receipt is under one million won — about 700 dollars —

11
00:01:22,000 --> 00:01:30,000
the store takes the tax off right at the counter.

12
00:01:30,000 --> 00:01:40,000
Look for a "Tax Free" sticker near the register.

13
00:01:40,000 --> 00:01:52,000
You must show your physical passport — not a photo on your phone.

14
00:01:52,000 --> 00:02:05,000
One tip: your purchase has to be at least fifteen thousand won to qualify.

15
00:02:05,000 --> 00:02:30,000
Almost any real outfit will count.

16
00:02:30,000 --> 00:02:45,000
What if your receipt is over a million won? Use the airport refund.

17
00:02:45,000 --> 00:03:00,000
Step one: keep every tax-free receipt the store gives you.

18
00:03:00,000 --> 00:03:18,000
Step two: at the airport, before checking bags, scan your receipts and passport at the kiosk.

19
00:03:18,000 --> 00:03:35,000
For bigger items, customs may want to see the goods — don't pack them too deep.

20
00:03:35,000 --> 00:04:00,000
Step three: collect your refund, in cash or back on your card.

21
00:04:00,000 --> 00:04:15,000
Now the honest part. That sticker says ten percent —

22
00:04:15,000 --> 00:04:30,000
but after service fees, you actually get about four to seven percent back.

23
00:04:30,000 --> 00:04:45,000
On a hundred-dollar jacket, that's four to seven dollars.

24
00:04:45,000 --> 00:05:00,000
Small per item — but across a trip, it's a whole extra outfit.

25
00:05:00,000 --> 00:05:20,000
So where should you shop? Seongsu, Hongdae, and Myeongdong —

26
00:05:20,000 --> 00:05:35,000
the big flagships and concept stores usually do instant refunds.

27
00:05:35,000 --> 00:06:00,000
